  <metadata>
    <name>Continental Divide Trail (SOBO)</name>
    <desc>Southbound from the Waterton Lake border monument. 3,029.0 miles of CDTC centreline with GLO-30 elevation, 32 alternates.</desc>
    <author><name>Continental Divide Trail Coalition</name></author>
    <keywords>Continental Divide Trail Coalition centreline, CC BY. Elevation: Copernicus GLO-30 (ESA/DLR, free for any use with attribution). Built by cdt-data.</keywords>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="48.998682" lon="-113.906057">
    <ele>1286.7</ele>
    <name>Northern terminus - Waterton Lake</name>
    <desc>mi 0.0 (SOBO mi 0.0) | off. mi 0.0 | Montana | MT (not on an extracted map page) | The border monument on the west shore of Upper Waterton Lake. Southbound mile 0; northbound finish. Reached by boat or on foot from Goat Haunt.</desc>
    <type>endpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.998682" lon="-113.906057">
    <ele>1286.7</ele>
    <name>Great Divide Trail (Waterton) leaves the CDT</name>
    <desc>mi 0.0 (SOBO mi 0.0) | off. mi 0.0 | MT | MT (not on an extracted map page) | Great Divide Trail (Waterton): 4 mi against 0 mi on the CDT, +921 ft. The first 4.2 miles of Canada&apos;s Great Divide Trail, north from the Waterton border monument. Not part of the CDT.</desc>
    <type>junction</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.998682" lon="-113.906057">
    <ele>1286.7</ele>
    <name>Waterton Park (Alberta) (access: Waterton Lake border monument (Goat Haunt))</name>
    <desc>mi 0.0 (SOBO mi 0.0) | off. mi 0.0 | MT | MT (not on an extracted map page) | Leave the CDT here for Waterton Park (Alberta): 8.7 mi by shuttle. Northern terminus town, in Canada. Rocky Mountain Foodmart is the only grocery and it is a small tourist-season convenience store; hotels, restaurants and a Parks Canada campground.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.051328" lon="-113.908306">
    <ele>1280.2</ele>
    <name>Waterton Park (Alberta)</name>
    <desc>mi 0.0 (SOBO mi 0.0) | off. mi 0.0 | MT | MT (not on an extracted map page) | Northern terminus town, in Canada. Rocky Mountain Foodmart is the only grocery and it is a small tourist-season convenience store; hotels, restaurants and a Parks Canada campground. Reached from the Waterton Lake border monument (mile 0 SOBO) by the Waterton Shoreline Cruise or by walking the Waterton Lakeshore Trail, roughly 8.7 miles. Entering Canada on foot at Goat Haunt requires prior authorisation; SOBO hikers who start here and NOBO hikers who finish here both need it, and hikers without it use the Chief Mountain route instead. Canada Post, not USPS, so the US general-delivery convention does not apply. Post office: 209 Fountain Avenue, Waterton Park, AB T0K 2M0. 8.7 mi off trail by shuttle. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.916684" lon="-113.905448">
    <ele>1378.6</ele>
    <name>Official mile 3030</name>
    <desc>mi 7.9 (SOBO mi 7.9) | off. mi 7.9 | MT | MT (not on an extracted map page) | CDTC official mile 3030, counted northbound from Crazy Cook. Official SOBO mile 7.9; geometric SOBO mile 7.9. North of the last published marker: this number is extrapolated.</desc>
    <type>milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.844229" lon="-113.82698">
    <ele>2086.4</ele>
    <name>Babb (access: Chief Mountain border crossing (US 17 / MT 17))</name>
    <desc>mi 17.1 (SOBO mi 17.1) | off. mi 17.1 | MT | MT (not on an extracted map page) | Leave the CDT here for Babb: 14 mi by hitching. Thronson&apos;s General Store, motel and cafe on US 89, the only services on the Chief Mountain route. A small store: snacks, fuel, cold drinks, not a shop you can plan a five-day carry around.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.860019" lon="-113.436792">
    <ele>1341.1</ele>
    <name>Babb</name>
    <desc>mi 17.1 (SOBO mi 17.1) | off. mi 17.1 | MT | MT (not on an extracted map page) | Thronson&apos;s General Store, motel and cafe on US 89, the only services on the Chief Mountain route. A small store: snacks, fuel, cold drinks, not a shop you can plan a five-day carry around. Post office is a hundred metres north. Used mainly by hikers finishing or starting at the Chief Mountain border crossing rather than at Waterton. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 4016 US Highway 89, Babb, MT 59411 (general delivery). 14 mi off trail by hitching. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.833815" lon="-113.827605">
    <ele>1925.4</ele>
    <name>Official mile 3020</name>
