  <wpt lat="48.800083" lon="-113.656936">
    <ele>1488.9</ele>
    <name>Chief Mountain Route leaves the CDT</name>
    <desc>mi 35.1 (SOBO mi 35.1) | off. mi 35.1 | MT | MT (not on an extracted map page) | Chief Mountain Route: 26.1 mi against 18 mi on the CDT, +4,274 ft. Alternate northern terminus. Leaves the CDT at the Belly River / Chief Mountain junction in Glacier NP and runs to the Chief Mountain port of entry on MT 17, the only CDT border crossing with a road and a customs post. Ley&apos;s MT 1 note 2 sends hikers this way for the easier logistics and for Stoney Indian Pass. Also mapped by OSM as relation 7873429 and by Ley&apos;s 2010 master as Alternate1.</desc>
    <type>junction</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.797877" lon="-113.676932">
    <ele>1493.5</ele>
    <name>Many Glacier (Swiftcurrent)</name>
    <desc>mi 35.4 (SOBO mi 35.4) | off. mi 35.4 | MT | MT (not on an extracted map page) | Camp store at the Swiftcurrent Motor Inn, with a restaurant next door that opens early and closes late. About 17% of 2026 thru-hikers used it. Basic but adequate for a two- or three-day carry if you are not fussy. The trail passes Many Glacier Hotel a mile east; walk the road round the lake. Seasonal - closed outside roughly June to mid-September, which matters for late SOBO starts and early NOBO finishes. 1 mi off trail on foot. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.769312" lon="-113.683042">
    <ele>1558</ele>
    <name>Official mile 3000</name>
