  <wpt lat="48.484867" lon="-113.369873">
    <ele>1575.8</ele>
    <name>Two Medicine</name>
    <desc>mi 88.8 (SOBO mi 88.8) | off. mi 88.8 | MT | MT (not on an extracted map page) | Two Medicine General Store, in the historic chalet building on the lake, right on the trail. Snacks, drinks, a little camp food; no restaurant. Around 4.5% of 2026 hikers counted it as a resupply. The front-country campground was closed for construction in 2026 with a temporary backcountry site in its place, per the NPS - check before relying on camping here. 0.1 mi off trail along the trail. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.453634" lon="-113.252467">
    <ele>1566.7</ele>
    <name>Official mile 2940</name>
    <desc>mi 97.9 (SOBO mi 97.9) | off. mi 97.9 | MT | MT (not on an extracted map page) | CDTC official mile 2940, counted northbound from Crazy Cook. Official SOBO mile 97.9; geometric SOBO mile 97.9. North of the last published marker: this number is extrapolated.</desc>
    <type>milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.44181" lon="-113.218196">
    <ele>1463</ele>
    <name>East Glacier Park</name>
    <desc>mi 99.5 (SOBO mi 99.5) | off. mi 99.5 | MT | MT (not on an extracted map page) | The Montana terminus town: 95% of 2026 thru-hikers resupplied here, more than anywhere else on the trail. But there is no supermarket - Glacier Park Trading Company and the Cenex travel centre are convenience stores, so this is a limited resupply despite its popularity, and hikers who want a real grocery hitch to Browning. Post office takes general delivery and is the standard box drop for the northern terminus. Restaurants, Amtrak&apos;s Empire Builder, and two hostels. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 15 Blackfoot Avenue, East Glacier Park, MT 59434 (general delivery). 0.5 mi off trail along the trail. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <link href="http://www.seeglacier.com/glacier-park-trading-company/" />
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.448563" lon="-113.225151">
    <ele>1474.2</ele>
    <name>Brownie&apos;s Hostel, East Glacier</name>
    <desc>mi 99.5 (SOBO mi 99.5) | off. mi 99.5 | MT | MT (not on an extracted map page) | Hiker hostel above the bakery on MT 49, the standard East Glacier stop. Bunks and private rooms. Confirm box-holding by phone before sending - a hostel is not a post office and cannot redirect a package. Accepts resupply boxes. 0.4 mi off trail on foot. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <link href="https://brownieshostel.com/" />
    <type>accommodation</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.444416" lon="-113.225364">
    <ele>1461.7</ele>
    <name>Browning (access: CDT through East Glacier Park)</name>
    <desc>mi 99.5 (SOBO mi 99.5) | off. mi 99.5 | MT | MT (not on an extracted map page) | Leave the CDT here for Browning: 13 mi by hitching. Teeple&apos;s IGA and Glacier Family Foods are the first full supermarkets south of the border, 13 miles east of East Glacier on US 2 on the Blackfeet Nation.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.556301" lon="-113.016736">
    <ele>1341.1</ele>
    <name>Browning</name>
    <desc>mi 99.5 (SOBO mi 99.5) | off. mi 99.5 | MT | MT (not on an extracted map page) | Teeple&apos;s IGA and Glacier Family Foods are the first full supermarkets south of the border, 13 miles east of East Glacier on US 2 on the Blackfeet Nation. Not a traditional CDT stop - most hikers make do with East Glacier&apos;s convenience stores - but it is the only proper grocery for a very long way in either direction. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 316 North Piegan Street, Browning, MT 59417 (general delivery). 13 mi off trail by hitching. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
