    <ele>1729.2</ele>
    <name>Lincoln (access: Rogers Pass (MT 200))</name>
    <desc>mi 291.0 (SOBO mi 291.0) | off. mi 291.0 | MT | MT map 378 | Leave the CDT here for Lincoln: 15 mi by hitching. CDTC Gateway Community. D &amp; D Foodtown is a small supermarket, and there is a co-op, a hardware-and-general store, several motels and bars.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.955454" lon="-112.680589">
    <ele>1389.9</ele>
    <name>Lincoln</name>
    <desc>mi 291.0 (SOBO mi 291.0) | off. mi 291.0 | MT | MT map 378 | CDTC Gateway Community. D &amp; D Foodtown is a small supermarket, and there is a co-op, a hardware-and-general store, several motels and bars. The last town before the long Bob Marshall carry to East Glacier, which is why almost everyone stops. Reached from Rogers Pass on MT 200, about 15 miles west; the Stemple Pass road, 14 miles further south along the trail, is the alternative and is quieter. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 237 Main Street, Lincoln, MT 59639 (general delivery). 15 mi off trail by hitching. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
