  <wpt lat="46.208313" lon="-112.57593">
    <ele>2074.9</ele>
    <name>Anaconda Cutoff branches</name>
    <desc>mi 409.1 (SOBO mi 409.1) | off. mi 409.3 | MT | MT map 363 | Anaconda Cutoff: 53 mi against 148.2 mi on the CDT, +5,496 ft. The best known Montana cutoff: leaves the CDT near Champion Pass / MT 30-31, drops through Anaconda and rejoins near Storm Lake, skipping the whole Butte loop. 53 mi in OSM (relation 8107272, sub-relations 8106945 + 8107271, tagged ref:xref &apos;MT ley=31a.31b.31c.31d.31e.43&apos;). Ley&apos;s own view (MT 31 general note): &apos;Many people hike this cutoff, but it really does miss some nice and new sections of trail around Butte... certainly nicer than the Anaconda Cutoff.&apos; Ley&apos;s 2010 master maps the same line as Alternate23 (50.9 mi).</desc>
    <type>junction</type>
  </wpt>
