  <wpt lat="46.040674" lon="-113.046581">
    <ele>2391.2</ele>
    <name>Anaconda (access: CDT primary route nearest Anaconda (Anaconda-Pintler))</name>
    <desc>mi 531.3 (SOBO mi 531.3) | off. mi 532.0 | MT | MT map 350 | Leave the CDT here for Anaconda: 14 mi by hitching. CDTC Gateway Community, and described by hikers as the best town between Colorado and Glacier. Albertsons, motels, a hostel, restaurants.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.127018" lon="-112.935243">
    <ele>1626.1</ele>
    <name>Anaconda</name>
    <desc>mi 531.3 (SOBO mi 531.3) | off. mi 532.0 | MT | MT map 350 | CDTC Gateway Community, and described by hikers as the best town between Colorado and Glacier. Albertsons, motels, a hostel, restaurants. The Anaconda Cut-off alternate walks straight through the town centre and skips roughly 90 miles of the primary route including Butte, which is why most hikers see Anaconda rather than Butte; from the primary route it is about 14 miles by road. accessFrom here is the primary route&apos;s nearest approach, so a plan built on the Cut-off will show a longer detour than you actually walk. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 218 Main Street, Anaconda, MT 59711 (general delivery). 14 mi off trail by hitching. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
