    <name>Lima (access: Monida Pass (I-15))</name>
    <desc>mi 854.4 (SOBO mi 854.4) | off. mi 856.5 | MT | MT map 308 | Leave the CDT here for Lima: 15 mi by hitching. CDTC Gateway Community, and a box town: one unnamed store attached to the gas station, Jan&apos;s Cafe, and the post office. Most hikers send a package.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.635202" lon="-112.592029">
    <ele>1905</ele>
    <name>Lima</name>
    <desc>mi 854.4 (SOBO mi 854.4) | off. mi 856.5 | MT | MT map 308 | CDTC Gateway Community, and a box town: one unnamed store attached to the gas station, Jan&apos;s Cafe, and the post office. Most hikers send a package. The Mountain View Motel runs a shuttle, holds packages, and sells showers and hammock space cheaply. Fifteen miles up I-15 from Monida Pass; the trail also passes about 9 miles east of town over the Lima Peaks, which is the shorter but rougher way out. Coordinate is the post office. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 700 Peat Street, Lima, MT 59739 (general delivery). 15 mi off trail by hitching. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
