  <wpt lat="43.16918" lon="-109.741905">
    <ele>2939</ele>
    <name>Knapsack Col branches</name>
    <desc>mi 1178.8 (SOBO mi 1178.8) | off. mi 1182.0 | WY | WY map 265 | Knapsack Col: 13.2 mi against 13.9 mi on the CDT, +3,660 ft. OSM relation 8094502 (ref:cdtc &apos;WY bcs 14&apos;), 10.2 mi. Leaves the CDT at the Green River and crosses Knapsack Col into Titcomb Basin. Ley: &apos;possibly one of the most amazing places along the CDT. It does require some rough scrambling east of the Col... there is a bit of rapidly melting glacier.&apos; OSM relation extract repaired: the relation is missing the ways that carry the route across a 3.8 km hole at 43.1330, -109.6386, so that stretch was routed over OSM highway ways 250206148, 971336802, 1308382530, 1317027759, 1553668694 (5.0 km) fetched separately from Overpass. The joined line is 13.3 mi and attaches 0 m / 2 m from the primary line; `data/external/osm-joined/knapsack-col.geojson` is the file the build reads, and `data/external/osm/` still holds the untouched relation extract. The hole is Knapsack Col itself, which OSM does carry as a path.</desc>
