  <wpt lat="42.79521" lon="-109.303147">
    <ele>3041.1</ele>
    <name>Cirque of the Towers branches</name>
    <desc>mi 1225.1 (SOBO mi 1225.1) | off. mi 1228.5 | WY | WY map 257 | Cirque of the Towers: 14.8 mi against 8.4 mi on the CDT, +2,557 ft. OSM relation 8094418 (ref:cdtc &apos;WY bcs=12.13 ley=19.20&apos;), 25.3 mi. Leaves the CDT at Big Sandy, crosses Jackass Pass into the Cirque and returns over Texas Pass and Temple Pass. The most-walked alternate in Wyoming. Ley: &apos;You might find that much of this route has tread. Highly recommended if you can swing it logistically!&apos;</desc>
    <type>junction</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.69574" lon="-109.266675">
    <ele>2790.2</ele>
    <name>Big Sandy Lodge (access: CDT at Big Sandy trailhead)</name>
    <desc>mi 1233.4 (SOBO mi 1233.4) | off. mi 1236.8 | WY | WY map 256 | Leave the CDT here for Big Sandy Lodge: 1.2 mi on foot. A backcountry lodge at the Big Sandy trailhead, on the southern edge of the Wind Rivers, that advertises CDT resupply pickups along with hot showers, beds and home-cooked meals.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.682471" lon="-109.280273">
    <ele>2773.7</ele>
    <name>Big Sandy Lodge</name>
    <desc>mi 1233.4 (SOBO mi 1233.4) | off. mi 1236.8 | WY | WY map 256 | A backcountry lodge at the Big Sandy trailhead, on the southern edge of the Wind Rivers, that advertises CDT resupply pickups along with hot showers, beds and home-cooked meals. No shop - it is a box drop with food and a bed attached, and you must arrange it in advance. Reservations essential; there is no drop-in service. Accepts resupply boxes. 1.2 mi off trail on foot. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <link href="https://www.big-sandy-lodge.com/" />
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.69574" lon="-109.266675">
    <ele>2790.2</ele>
    <name>Boulder (access: CDT at Big Sandy trailhead)</name>
    <desc>mi 1233.4 (SOBO mi 1233.4) | off. mi 1236.8 | WY | WY map 256 | Leave the CDT here for Boulder: 35 mi by hitching. The Boulder Store and post office on US 191, a crossroads settlement between Big Sandy and Pinedale. Minor: a convenience store, useful only if you are hitching this stretch of highway anyway and cannot get to Pinedale.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.746652" lon="-109.720581">
    <ele>2158</ele>
    <name>Boulder</name>
    <desc>mi 1233.4 (SOBO mi 1233.4) | off. mi 1236.8 | WY | WY map 256 | The Boulder Store and post office on US 191, a crossroads settlement between Big Sandy and Pinedale. Minor: a convenience store, useful only if you are hitching this stretch of highway anyway and cannot get to Pinedale. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 7 State Highway 353, Boulder, WY 82923 (general delivery). 35 mi off trail by hitching. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.694863" lon="-109.264843">
    <ele>2784.9</ele>
    <name>Cirque of the Towers rejoins</name>
    <desc>mi 1233.5 (SOBO mi 1233.5) | off. mi 1237.0 | WY | WY map 256 | Cirque of the Towers: 14.8 mi against 8.4 mi on the CDT, +2,557 ft. OSM relation 8094418 (ref:cdtc &apos;WY bcs=12.13 ley=19.20&apos;), 25.3 mi. Leaves the CDT at Big Sandy, crosses Jackass Pass into the Cirque and returns over Texas Pass and Temple Pass. The most-walked alternate in Wyoming. Ley: &apos;You might find that much of this route has tread. Highly recommended if you can swing it logistically!&apos;</desc>
    <type>junction</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.689474" lon="-109.263731">
    <ele>2810.7</ele>
    <name>Wind River High Route (Dixon variation) rejoins</name>
    <desc>mi 1234.0 (SOBO mi 1234.0) | off. mi 1237.4 | WY | WY map 256 | Wind River High Route (Dixon variation): 78.8 mi against 70.2 mi on the CDT, +16,974 ft. Alan Dixon&apos;s variation of the Wind River High Route: off-trail, above treeline, and not a trail in any maintained sense.</desc>
    <type>junction</type>
  </wpt>
