  <wpt lat="42.462223" lon="-108.851118">
    <ele>2456.9</ele>
    <name>Famous Alternate (Lander to Old Faithful) rejoins</name>
    <desc>mi 1275.6 (SOBO mi 1275.6) | off. mi 1279.3 | WY | WY map 250 | Famous Alternate (Lander to Old Faithful): 383.5 mi against 270.8 mi on the CDT, +71,137 ft. SeekingLost&apos;s 2018 Wind River / Tetons / Yellowstone variant: Lander to Dubois, Dubois to Jackson, Jackson to Flagg Ranch, Flagg Ranch to Old Faithful. Walked northbound, so the file is reversed for the southbound build.</desc>
    <type>junction</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.46946" lon="-108.80209">
    <ele>2377.4</ele>
    <name>South Pass City</name>
    <desc>mi 1278.4 (SOBO mi 1278.4) | off. mi 1282.1 | WY | WY map 250 | A restored gold-rush town, now a state historic site, that the trail runs straight through. Named by CDTC as a Gateway Community jointly with Lander. There is no shop and no post office - a visitor centre, sometimes a cafe in season, and water. Coordinate is the CDTC Gateway Communities layer&apos;s point for the site; OpenStreetMap has no shop or post office here. 0.2 mi off trail along the trail. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>food</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.477776" lon="-108.774192">
    <ele>2454.8</ele>
    <name>Lander (access: WY 28 at South Pass)</name>
    <desc>mi 1280.7 (SOBO mi 1280.7) | off. mi 1284.4 | WY | WY map 250 | Leave the CDT here for Lander: 35 mi by hitching. CDTC Gateway Community (with South Pass City) and a full resupply: Safeway, Mr. D&apos;s Food Center, gear shops, NOLS, motels.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.837834" lon="-108.74648">
    <ele>1632.8</ele>
    <name>Lander</name>
    <desc>mi 1280.7 (SOBO mi 1280.7) | off. mi 1284.4 | WY | WY map 250 | CDTC Gateway Community (with South Pass City) and a full resupply: Safeway, Mr. D&apos;s Food Center, gear shops, NOLS, motels. Bear spray is easy to buy here, which matters for everyone heading north into the Wind Rivers and Yellowstone. Thirty-five miles from the WY 28 crossing at South Pass and a well-travelled hitch. The USGS post-office dataset does not cover Lander; the street address here is the one the hiker guides publish. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 230 Grandview Drive, Lander, WY 82520 (general delivery). 35 mi off trail by hitching. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
