    <name>Jeffrey City (access: CDT in the Great Divide Basin nearest US 287)</name>
    <desc>mi 1334.4 (SOBO mi 1334.4) | off. mi 1338.3 | WY | WY map 241 | Leave the CDT here for Jeffrey City: 12 mi by hitching. A near-abandoned uranium town on US 287 whose Split Rock Bar and Cafe is the only thing open, and the only building of any kind for a long way along the Great Divide Basin road walk. A meal and water, not a resupply.</desc>
    <type>food</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.493891" lon="-107.825074">
    <ele>1920.2</ele>
    <name>Jeffrey City</name>
    <desc>mi 1334.4 (SOBO mi 1334.4) | off. mi 1338.3 | WY | WY map 241 | A near-abandoned uranium town on US 287 whose Split Rock Bar and Cafe is the only thing open, and the only building of any kind for a long way along the Great Divide Basin road walk. A meal and water, not a resupply. Hikers on the trail proper are about 10 miles south of it; hikers on the highway alternate walk past the door. 12 mi off trail by hitching. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>food</type>
  </wpt>
