    <name>Bridger Pass bypass (Rawlins shortcut) branches</name>
    <desc>mi 1411.7 (SOBO mi 1411.7) | off. mi 1415.6 | WY | WY map 227 | Bridger Pass bypass (Rawlins shortcut): 23.2 mi against 41.4 mi on the CDT, +1,589 ft. OSM relation 8097777 (ref:cdtc &apos;WY ley=37a.37b.40&apos;), 23.3 mi, both ends within 5 m of the primary line. Ley&apos;s WY 37 note 3: &apos;An alternate here by-passes Bridger Pass, cutting off about 15-20 miles, shown on maps 37a-b. This route re-connects on map WY40.&apos; WY 40 note 3 calls it a shortcut to/from Rawlins, &apos;still over 30 miles total, but much of it is paved&apos;.</desc>
