  <wpt lat="40.311082" lon="-105.811918">
    <ele>2872.2</ele>
    <name>Tonahutu Creek (RMNP loop) branches</name>
    <desc>mi 1636.6 (SOBO mi 1636.6) | off. mi 1641.4 | CO | CO map 194 | Tonahutu Creek (RMNP loop): 4.3 mi against 21.9 mi on the CDT, +97 ft. The CDTC publishes a 4.4 mi &apos;CDT Tonahutu Creek Route&apos; north of Grand Lake; Ley&apos;s CO 10a maps the full loop: &apos;This map shows the Rocky Mountain National Park (RMNP) loop. It&apos;s about 25 miles and quite spectacular... You can leave your stuff in Grand Lake, and slack-pack a big loop (including Tonahutu Creek).&apos; A backcountry permit is required to camp. The CDTC geometry is only the northern link - the rest still needs tracing from CO 10a.</desc>
    <type>junction</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="40.329275" lon="-105.734264">
    <ele>3446.9</ele>
    <name>Official mile 1390</name>
