    <ele>2608.9</ele>
    <name>Tonahutu Creek (RMNP loop) rejoins</name>
    <desc>mi 1658.5 (SOBO mi 1658.5) | off. mi 1663.5 | CO | CO map 192 | Tonahutu Creek (RMNP loop): 4.3 mi against 21.9 mi on the CDT, +97 ft. The CDTC publishes a 4.4 mi &apos;CDT Tonahutu Creek Route&apos; north of Grand Lake; Ley&apos;s CO 10a maps the full loop: &apos;This map shows the Rocky Mountain National Park (RMNP) loop. It&apos;s about 25 miles and quite spectacular... You can leave your stuff in Grand Lake, and slack-pack a big loop (including Tonahutu Creek).&apos; A backcountry permit is required to camp. The CDTC geometry is only the northern link - the rest still needs tracing from CO 10a.</desc>
    <type>junction</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="40.252979" lon="-105.829256">
    <ele>2550.9</ele>
    <name>Grand Lake</name>
    <desc>mi 1659.5 (SOBO mi 1659.5) | off. mi 1664.5 | CO | CO map 191 | CDTC Gateway Community, on the trail at the western edge of Rocky Mountain National Park. Mountain Food Market is a small but real grocery on Grand Avenue; motels, restaurants, a hostel. This is also where you sort out RMNP backcountry permits, which are quota-limited and worth arranging well ahead. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 520 Center Drive, Grand Lake, CO 80447 (general delivery). 0.4 mi off trail along the trail. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="40.250078" lon="-105.826023">
    <ele>2555.2</ele>
    <name>Granby (access: CDT at Grand Lake)</name>
    <desc>mi 1659.5 (SOBO mi 1659.5) | off. mi 1664.5 | CO | CO map 191 | Leave the CDT here for Granby: 15 mi by hitching. City Market on Thompson Road, fifteen miles down US 34 from Grand Lake. Larger and cheaper than Grand Lake&apos;s grocery, and the alternative for hikers who want a full shop and do not mind the extra hitch.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="40.062774" lon="-105.92941">
    <ele>2418.6</ele>
    <name>Granby</name>
    <desc>mi 1659.5 (SOBO mi 1659.5) | off. mi 1664.5 | CO | CO map 191 | City Market on Thompson Road, fifteen miles down US 34 from Grand Lake. Larger and cheaper than Grand Lake&apos;s grocery, and the alternative for hikers who want a full shop and do not mind the extra hitch. Not a traditional CDT stop. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 54 Zero Street, Granby, CO 80446 (general delivery). 15 mi off trail by hitching. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
