  <wpt lat="39.539701" lon="-106.05922">
    <ele>2987.6</ele>
    <name>Silverthorne (access: CDT / Colorado Trail near CO 9, Tenmile Range)</name>
    <desc>mi 1793.1 (SOBO mi 1793.1) | off. mi 1798.9 | CO | CO map 175 | Leave the CDT here for Silverthorne: 8 mi by hitching. Full resupply in the Summit County cluster. The City Market that serves Silverthorne is across the Blue River in Dillon, about a mile south-east of the Silverthorne post office at 518 Brian Avenue; there is also a…</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="39.63042" lon="-106.055431">
    <ele>2660.9</ele>
    <name>Silverthorne</name>
    <desc>mi 1793.1 (SOBO mi 1793.1) | off. mi 1798.9 | CO | CO map 175 | Full resupply in the Summit County cluster. The City Market that serves Silverthorne is across the Blue River in Dillon, about a mile south-east of the Silverthorne post office at 518 Brian Avenue; there is also a Target and outlet shopping. Reached from the CDT/Colorado Trail near the Gore Range, about 8 miles east on CO 9, and a Summit Stage bus links Silverthorne, Frisco, Breckenridge and Copper Mountain free of charge - so hitting one of these four is really hitting all of them. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 518 Brian Avenue, Silverthorne, CO 80497 (general delivery). 8 mi off trail by hitching. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="39.489026" lon="-106.11276">
    <ele>3703.2</ele>
    <name>Breckenridge (access: Gold Hill trailhead (CO 9))</name>
    <desc>mi 1801.9 (SOBO mi 1801.9) | off. mi 1807.8 | CO | CO map 174 | Leave the CDT here for Breckenridge: 4 mi by hitching. City Market at the north end of town, plus everything a ski resort has. Named by CDTC among the towns hikers use.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="39.488772" lon="-106.046892">
    <ele>2926.1</ele>
    <name>Breckenridge</name>
    <desc>mi 1801.9 (SOBO mi 1801.9) | off. mi 1807.8 | CO | CO map 174 | City Market at the north end of town, plus everything a ski resort has. Named by CDTC among the towns hikers use. Reached from the Gold Hill trailhead on CO 9, about 4 miles, or on the free Summit Stage from Copper Mountain. Expensive lodging in season. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 305 South Ridge Street, Breckenridge, CO 80424 (general delivery). 4 mi off trail by hitching. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="39.486866" lon="-106.113628">
