    <type>milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="39.495828" lon="-106.145937">
    <ele>3041</ele>
    <name>Frisco (access: CDT / Colorado Trail at Copper Mountain (CO 91))</name>
    <desc>mi 1806.4 (SOBO mi 1806.4) | off. mi 1812.3 | CO | CO map 174 | Leave the CDT here for Frisco: 8 mi by shuttle. Safeway, Whole Foods, Natural Grocers and a Walmart along Summit Boulevard - the best-stocked of the four Summit County towns and the closest to the trail.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="39.589848" lon="-106.096798">
    <ele>2772.8</ele>
    <name>Frisco</name>
    <desc>mi 1806.4 (SOBO mi 1806.4) | off. mi 1812.3 | CO | CO map 174 | Safeway, Whole Foods, Natural Grocers and a Walmart along Summit Boulevard - the best-stocked of the four Summit County towns and the closest to the trail. On the free Summit Stage bus network with Silverthorne, Breckenridge and Copper Mountain. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 35 West Main Street, Frisco, CO 80443 (general delivery). 8 mi off trail by shuttle. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="39.499349" lon="-106.152787">
    <ele>2974.2</ele>
    <name>Copper Mountain (access: CDT / Colorado Trail at Copper Mountain)</name>
    <desc>mi 1807.0 (SOBO mi 1807.0) | off. mi 1812.8 | CO | CO map 174 | Leave the CDT here for Copper Mountain: 0.8 mi on foot. The trail passes through the resort village at Copper Mountain. There is no grocery - a gas station convenience store and resort restaurants - but it is the free Summit Stage bus stop for Frisco, Silverthorne and…</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="39.506157" lon="-106.141094">
    <ele>2960.2</ele>
    <name>Copper Mountain</name>
    <desc>mi 1807.0 (SOBO mi 1807.0) | off. mi 1812.8 | CO | CO map 174 | The trail passes through the resort village at Copper Mountain. There is no grocery - a gas station convenience store and resort restaurants - but it is the free Summit Stage bus stop for Frisco, Silverthorne and Breckenridge, which is what makes it useful. Very quiet outside the ski season. 0.8 mi off trail on foot. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="39.498563" lon="-106.156087">
    <ele>2997</ele>
    <name>Grays and Torreys / Argentine Spine rejoins</name>
    <desc>mi 1807.2 (SOBO mi 1807.2) | off. mi 1813.0 | CO | CO map 174 | Grays and Torreys / Argentine Spine: 45.3 mi against 80.8 mi on the CDT, +10,310 ft. The &apos;official route&apos; over Grays and Torreys Peaks and along the Argentine Spine, from CO 15 to CO 18 via detail sheets CO 15a-d, versus Ley&apos;s red line through Silverthorne. OSM relation 8067605 &apos;CDT ij- Sliverthorn Route&apos; (ref:xref &apos;CO ley=15-18, cdtc=xxx&apos;), 48.8 mi, both ends within 35 m of the primary line. Ley: &apos;It does go over some dramatic topography, but also some roads. The red route is nice too, and more consistently on trail. Resupply is a little easier on the red route as it goes through Silverthorne. But there are free busses along the Grays-Torreys route.&apos; CO 15a note 4: &apos;This route is a knife edge with lots of exposure and steep cliffs.&apos;</desc>
    <type>junction</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="39.474336" lon="-106.218907">
