  <wpt lat="39.362171" lon="-106.31307">
    <ele>3196.2</ele>
    <name>Leadville (access: Tennessee Pass (US 24))</name>
    <desc>mi 1830.7 (SOBO mi 1830.7) | off. mi 1836.7 | CO | CO map 171 | Leave the CDT here for Leadville: 9 mi by hitching. CDTC Gateway Community (with Twin Lakes). Safeway on North Poplar, plus Tenderfoot Market and a general store downtown, hostels, motels and outfitters. Nine miles south of Tennessee Pass on US 24, an easy hitch.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="39.260034" lon="-106.293102">
    <ele>3094.3</ele>
    <name>Leadville</name>
    <desc>mi 1830.7 (SOBO mi 1830.7) | off. mi 1836.7 | CO | CO map 171 | CDTC Gateway Community (with Twin Lakes). Safeway on North Poplar, plus Tenderfoot Market and a general store downtown, hostels, motels and outfitters. Nine miles south of Tennessee Pass on US 24, an easy hitch. At 10,150 ft the highest incorporated town in the United States, which is worth knowing if you are arriving unacclimatised. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 130 West 5th Street, Leadville, CO 80461 (general delivery). 9 mi off trail by hitching. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
