  <wpt lat="35.320517" lon="-107.574245">
    <ele>2586.5</ele>
    <name>Mount Taylor summit branches</name>
    <desc>mi 2466.0 (SOBO mi 2466.0) | off. mi 2474.1 | NM | NM map 86 | Mount Taylor summit: 14.6 mi against 13.5 mi on the CDT, +3,449 ft. OSM relation 8078041 (ref:xref &apos;NM bcs=21,Ley=18,cdtc=xxx&apos;), 14.7 mi, both ends within 6 m of the primary line. The Forest Service designated the north-side bypass as the official route; Ley keeps the summit as his main line. NM 18 note 6: &apos;Some people hiked both routes recommend the Mt. Taylor summit (others prefer the official route)... The official route does have a lot of up/down, is longer, and drier.&apos; The mountain is sacred to the Navajo (Tsoodzil), Zuni and Acoma.</desc>
    <type>junction</type>
  </wpt>
