  <wpt lat="34.301704" lon="-108.13854">
    <ele>2343.7</ele>
    <name>Cebolla rejoins</name>
    <desc>mi 2606.4 (SOBO mi 2606.4) | off. mi 2614.8 | NM | NM map 63 | Cebolla: 86.1 mi against 110.8 mi on the CDT, +4,312 ft. OSM relation 8082741 &apos;Cebolla Route Grants to Pie Town&apos; (ref:ley &apos;NM 20,20b,20c,20d,20e,21,22,24,25,26&apos;), 86.1 mi, both ends within 20 m of the primary line. Runs down Cebolla Canyon on the east side of El Malpais; the sub-relations are 8082740 (jkcCC, Grants south), 8082889 (jkgCC) and 8082910 (jkjCC, into Pie Town).</desc>
    <type>junction</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="34.29803" lon="-108.133636">
    <ele>2376.2</ele>
    <name>Pie Town</name>
    <desc>mi 2606.4 (SOBO mi 2606.4) | off. mi 2614.8 | NM | NM map 63 | A box town: there is no grocery, only pie shops, and CDTC flags it as one of the places hikers should mail to. Post office hours are short - mornings only on weekdays and a two-hour window on Saturday - so time your arrival. The Toaster House, the donation-based hiker house on the corner, is in dispute between sources: a 2024 write-up says it has closed, while 2026 accounts describe it as still open, run by Nita Larronde&apos;s children since her death in 2023. Assume nothing and ask ahead. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 17 Frontage Road, Pie Town, NM 87827 (general delivery). 0.4 mi off trail along the trail. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="34.299168" lon="-108.138778">
    <ele>2376.2</ele>
    <name>The Toaster House, Pie Town</name>
    <desc>mi 2606.4 (SOBO mi 2606.4) | off. mi 2614.8 | NM | NM map 63 | The donation-based hiker and cyclist house at Pie Town, open to CDT and Great Divide Route travellers since 1982. Its founder Nita Larronde died in 2023 and her children have kept it going; one 2024 CDT guide nonetheless reports it closed. Sources disagree, so check current word before planning a night here. No services beyond shelter, a kitchen and a donation box. 0.4 mi off trail on foot. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>accommodation</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="34.301704" lon="-108.13854">
    <ele>2343.7</ele>
    <name>Top of the World Store (access: CDT at Pie Town (US 60))</name>
    <desc>mi 2606.4 (SOBO mi 2606.4) | off. mi 2614.8 | NM | NM map 63 | Leave the CDT here for Top of the World Store: 3 mi on foot. General store and laundromat on US 60 about three miles west of Pie Town, at mile marker 52. A supplement to Pie Town rather than a replacement, and useful mainly to hikers whose box did not arrive.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="34.2945" lon="-108.187">
    <ele>2347</ele>
    <name>Top of the World Store</name>
    <desc>mi 2606.4 (SOBO mi 2606.4) | off. mi 2614.8 | NM | NM map 63 | General store and laundromat on US 60 about three miles west of Pie Town, at mile marker 52. A supplement to Pie Town rather than a replacement, and useful mainly to hikers whose box did not arrive. There is no OpenStreetMap entry, so the coordinate is derived from the store&apos;s own description of its position on US 60 and is approximate to within about a mile - do not navigate to it. 3 mi off trail on foot. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <link href="https://topoftheworldland.com/store/index.html" />
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
