  <wpt lat="32.862618" lon="-108.289907">
    <ele>2020</ele>
    <name>Gila River rejoins</name>
    <desc>mi 2856.3 (SOBO mi 2856.3) | off. mi 2864.9 | NM | NM map 27 | Gila River: 106.1 mi against 178.2 mi on the CDT, +10,395 ft. The best-known CDT alternate. OSM relation 7917427 (ref:ley &apos;NM 30,31,32,33,34,35,36&apos;), 110.5 mi, both ends within 20 m of the primary line. Leaves the official Black Range (CDTA) route on NM 30 and runs Snow Lake - Middle Fork Gila - Gila Cliff Dwellings - lower Gila - Sapillo Creek, rejoining near NM 37. Ley: &apos;This route bypasses the Gila River Canyon and the cliff dwellings which are both pretty cool... hikers who&apos;ve done both the Gila (upper &amp; lower) AND the Black Range official route, describe both as great, but the Gila better.&apos; 85 river crossings between Snow Lake and Jordan Hot Springs; dangerous in spring runoff. Sub-relations: 7917330 jmhGR, 7836357 jmjGR, 7903380 jmlGR, 7903373 jocGR, 7903372 jofGR, 7903363 joiGR, 7903362 jolGR, 7917348 jooGR. OSM relation extract repaired: the relation is missing the ways that carry the route across a 1.3 km hole at 33.4822, -108.4786, so that stretch was routed over OSM highway ways 1456540997 (1.3 km) fetched separately from Overpass. The joined line is 106.6 mi and attaches 3 m / 16 m from the primary line; `data/external/osm-joined/gila-river.geojson` is the file the build reads, and `data/external/osm/` still holds the untouched relation extract. Five short spur chains totalling 5.1 mi (an old-route fragment near Willow Creek and two 3-point stubs) are left out of the joined line.</desc>
    <type>junction</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="32.845058" lon="-108.319792">
