  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="32.780796" lon="-108.282683">
    <ele>1817.7</ele>
    <name>Silver City alternate branches</name>
    <desc>mi 2868.1 (SOBO mi 2868.1) | off. mi 2876.7 | NM | NM map 26 | Silver City alternate: 29 mi against 36.6 mi on the CDT, +2,531 ft. OSM relation 7896111, 24.8 mi, both ends within 3 m of the primary line, noted &apos;Old CDT route. Now a Silver City alternate.&apos; Ley&apos;s NM 37b note 2: &apos;since the route dead-ends north of this point, you have to head to the east and take roads + hwy 180 into Silver City (about 13 miles beyond the east edge of this map).&apos; OSM relation extract repaired: the relation is missing the ways that carry the route across a 6.4 km hole at 32.7646, -108.2754, so that stretch was routed over OSM highway ways 769470466, 861279816, 1531242325 (6.9 km) fetched separately from Overpass. The joined line is 29.1 mi and attaches 1 m / 3 m from the primary line; `data/external/osm-joined/silver-city-alternate.geojson` is the file the build reads, and `data/external/osm/` still holds the untouched relation extract.</desc>
    <type>junction</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="32.778" lon="-108.273">
    <ele>1796.8</ele>
    <name>Silver City</name>
    <desc>mi 2868.1 (SOBO mi 2868.1) | off. mi 2876.7 | NM | NM map 26 | CDTC Gateway Community, on the trail, and the biggest town in southern New Mexico: the Silver City Food Basket downtown, a food co-op, Albertsons and a 24-hour Walmart out on the east side, gear shops, hostels, breweries. Where hikers commit to the Gila River alternate or the higher primary line. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 500 North Hudson Street, Silver City, NM 88061 (general delivery). 1 mi off trail along the trail. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
