    <ele>1757.6</ele>
    <name>Official mile 100</name>
    <desc>mi 2929.3 (SOBO mi 2929.3) | off. mi 2937.9 | NM | NM map 17 | CDTC official mile 100, counted northbound from Crazy Cook. Official SOBO mile 2937.9; geometric SOBO mile 2929.3.</desc>
    <type>milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="32.397003" lon="-108.679235">
    <ele>1309.5</ele>
    <name>Official mile 90</name>
    <desc>mi 2939.3 (SOBO mi 2939.3) | off. mi 2947.9 | NM | NM map 16 | CDTC official mile 90, counted northbound from Crazy Cook. Official SOBO mile 2947.9; geometric SOBO mile 2939.3.</desc>
    <type>milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="32.34439" lon="-108.710526">
    <ele>1293.9</ele>
    <name>Lordsburg</name>
    <desc>mi 2943.8 (SOBO mi 2943.8) | off. mi 2952.4 | NM | NM map 15 | CDTC Gateway Community (as Hidalgo County) and the town at the New Mexico end of the trail. Saucedo&apos;s Super Market on Main Street is a full grocery and is also where CDTC says to buy isobutane, calling ahead for stock. The CDTC southern-terminus shuttle picks up at 207 Shakespeare Street behind the Chamber at 06:15 for northbound starts, $175 per rider, booked at least seven days ahead on 719-749-1234. The KOA and the Econo Lodge both do hiker rates. Note that since 2026 the southernmost 1.1 miles of trail and the Crazy Cook monument sit inside a National Defense Area and need written US Army permission arranged weeks in advance. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 401 Shakespeare Street, Lordsburg, NM 88045 (general delivery). 0.5 mi off trail along the trail. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <link href="https://cdtcoalition.org/explore-the-trail/southern-terminus-shuttle/" />
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="32.329121" lon="-108.723026">
    <ele>1339</ele>
    <name>Lordsburg reroute (CDTC) branches</name>
    <desc>mi 2945.3 (SOBO mi 2945.3) | off. mi 2954.0 | NM | NM map 15 | Lordsburg reroute (CDTC): 0.3 mi against 0.2 mi on the CDT, +29 ft. CDTC&apos;s &apos;CDT_Lburg_reroute&apos; FeatureServer layer, 12.6 mi, both ends on the primary line. The BLM realignment south of Lordsburg that Ley&apos;s NM 39c note describes. https://services8.arcgis.com/WyuHwdftppQLa5KO/arcgis/rest/services/CDT_Lburg_reroute/FeatureServer</desc>
    <type>junction</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="32.326414" lon="-108.725062">
    <ele>1343.7</ele>
    <name>Lordsburg reroute (CDTC) rejoins</name>
    <desc>mi 2945.5 (SOBO mi 2945.5) | off. mi 2954.2 | NM | NM map 14 | Lordsburg reroute (CDTC): 0.3 mi against 0.2 mi on the CDT, +29 ft. CDTC&apos;s &apos;CDT_Lburg_reroute&apos; FeatureServer layer, 12.6 mi, both ends on the primary line. The BLM realignment south of Lordsburg that Ley&apos;s NM 39c note describes. https://services8.arcgis.com/WyuHwdftppQLa5KO/arcgis/rest/services/CDT_Lburg_reroute/FeatureServer</desc>
    <type>junction</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="32.283143" lon="-108.75366">
    <ele>1439.9</ele>
    <name>Official mile 80</name>
    <desc>mi 2949.2 (SOBO mi 2949.2) | off. mi 2957.9 | NM | NM map 14 | CDTC official mile 80, counted northbound from Crazy Cook. Official SOBO mile 2957.9; geometric SOBO mile 2949.2.</desc>
    <type>milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="32.26283" lon="-108.74166">
    <ele>1396.8</ele>
    <name>Animas Road water cache</name>
    <desc>mi 2951.0 (SOBO mi 2951.0) | off. mi 2959.7 | NM | NM map 14 | Northernmost of the five CDTC cache boxes in the Bootheel, and the last before Lordsburg northbound. CDTC shuttle riders get two gallons at each box included in the fare; hikers not riding the shuttle can buy a water service for $25 in season, or self-cache. Coordinates are CDTC&apos;s own. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <link href="https://cdtcoalition.org/explore-the-trail/southern-terminus-shuttle/" />
    <type>water</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="32.2027" lon="-108.65883">
    <ele>1382</ele>
    <name>Official mile 70</name>
    <desc>mi 2959.2 (SOBO mi 2959.2) | off. mi 2967.9 | NM | NM map 12 | CDTC official mile 70, counted northbound from Crazy Cook. Official SOBO mile 2967.9; geometric SOBO mile 2959.2.</desc>
    <type>milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="32.131205" lon="-108.6079">
    <ele>1366.3</ele>
    <name>Animas (access: CDT in the Animas Valley)</name>
    <desc>mi 2965.6 (SOBO mi 2965.6) | off. mi 2974.3 | NM | NM map 11 | Leave the CDT here for Animas: 20 mi by hitching. Bootheel Grocery and a post office on NM 338, west of the trail. Rarely used - Hachita is closer to the route - but it is the other settlement within reach of the Bootheel section, and the CDTC water-cache road out to…</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="31.951206" lon="-108.796995">
    <ele>1341.1</ele>
    <name>Animas</name>
    <desc>mi 2965.6 (SOBO mi 2965.6) | off. mi 2974.3 | NM | NM map 11 | Bootheel Grocery and a post office on NM 338, west of the trail. Rarely used - Hachita is closer to the route - but it is the other settlement within reach of the Bootheel section, and the CDTC water-cache road out to the Animas Road box runs from here. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 2415 State Highway 338, Animas, NM 88020 (general delivery). 20 mi off trail by hitching. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="32.102597" lon="-108.56401">
    <ele>1377.4</ele>
    <name>Official mile 60</name>
    <desc>mi 2969.2 (SOBO mi 2969.2) | off. mi 2977.9 | NM | NM map 11 | CDTC official mile 60, counted northbound from Crazy Cook. Official SOBO mile 2977.9; geometric SOBO mile 2969.2.</desc>
    <type>milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="32.08053" lon="-108.55637">
    <ele>1365.3</ele>
    <name>Highway 113 water cache</name>
    <desc>mi 2970.9 (SOBO mi 2970.9) | off. mi 2979.6 | NM | NM map 10 | CDTC cache box in the Bootheel, on NM 113. Stocked for shuttle riders and for the paid water service; otherwise self-cache. Coordinates are CDTC&apos;s own. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <link href="https://cdtcoalition.org/explore-the-trail/southern-terminus-shuttle/" />
    <type>water</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="32.005825" lon="-108.469065">
    <ele>1451.1</ele>
    <name>Official mile 50</name>
    <desc>mi 2979.2 (SOBO mi 2979.2) | off. mi 2987.9 | NM | NM map 9 | CDTC official mile 50, counted northbound from Crazy Cook. Official SOBO mile 2987.9; geometric SOBO mile 2979.2.</desc>
    <type>milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="31.96518" lon="-108.43988">
    <ele>1430.2</ele>
    <name>Highway 9 water cache</name>
    <desc>mi 2983.7 (SOBO mi 2983.7) | off. mi 2992.5 | NM | NM map 8 | CDTC cache box where the trail meets NM 9 in the Bootheel, the nearest cache to Hachita. Stocked for shuttle riders and for the paid water service; otherwise self-cache. Coordinates are CDTC&apos;s own. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <link href="https://cdtcoalition.org/explore-the-trail/southern-terminus-shuttle/" />
    <type>water</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="31.909698" lon="-108.413058">
    <ele>1436.2</ele>
    <name>Official mile 40</name>
    <desc>mi 2989.1 (SOBO mi 2989.1) | off. mi 2997.9 | NM | NM map 7 | CDTC official mile 40, counted northbound from Crazy Cook. Official SOBO mile 2997.9; geometric SOBO mile 2989.1.</desc>
    <type>milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="31.88816" lon="-108.42268">
    <ele>1458.2</ele>
    <name>Hachita (access: CDT at NM 9)</name>
    <desc>mi 2990.8 (SOBO mi 2990.8) | off. mi 2999.6 | NM | NM map 7 | Leave the CDT here for Hachita: 5 mi by hitching. The Hachita Food Mart and post office on NM 9, and the only settlement in the Bootheel. A small convenience store with long hours, which counts for a great deal out here. Post office is on 575-483-2075 per CDTC.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="31.918449" lon="-108.325071">
    <ele>1359.4</ele>
    <name>Hachita</name>
    <desc>mi 2990.8 (SOBO mi 2990.8) | off. mi 2999.6 | NM | NM map 7 | The Hachita Food Mart and post office on NM 9, and the only settlement in the Bootheel. A small convenience store with long hours, which counts for a great deal out here. Post office is on 575-483-2075 per CDTC. About five miles east of where the trail meets NM 9, and directly on the Columbus alternate road walk. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: 26 B Street, Hachita, NM 88040 (general delivery). 5 mi off trail by hitching. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="31.88816" lon="-108.42268">
    <ele>1458.2</ele>
    <name>Columbus (access: CDT at NM 9)</name>
    <desc>mi 2990.8 (SOBO mi 2990.8) | off. mi 2999.6 | NM | NM map 7 | Leave the CDT here for Columbus: 45 mi on foot. The alternate southern terminus: a border village on NM 11 opposite Palomas, Mexico, reached by walking NM 9 east from the Hachita area instead of turning south to Crazy Cook.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="31.831226" lon="-107.634634">
    <ele>1236</ele>
    <name>Columbus</name>
    <desc>mi 2990.8 (SOBO mi 2990.8) | off. mi 2999.6 | NM | NM map 7 | The alternate southern terminus: a border village on NM 11 opposite Palomas, Mexico, reached by walking NM 9 east from the Hachita area instead of turning south to Crazy Cook. The San Jose Store and a Dollar General are the shops. Hikers choose this ending to avoid the Crazy Cook shuttle and, since 2026, the Fort Huachuca permission the National Defense Area now requires. Long, hot, waterless road walking with no shade. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: Columbus, NM 88029 (general delivery). 45 mi off trail on foot. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>resupply</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="31.88816" lon="-108.42268">
    <ele>1458.2</ele>
    <name>Deming (access: CDT at NM 9)</name>
    <desc>mi 2990.8 (SOBO mi 2990.8) | off. mi 2999.6 | NM | NM map 7 | Leave the CDT here for Deming: 55 mi by hitching. A 24-hour Walmart Supercenter, several dollar stores and motels on I-10, thirty miles north of Columbus on NM 11.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="32.270573" lon="-107.747232">
    <ele>1321.3</ele>
    <name>Deming</name>
    <desc>mi 2990.8 (SOBO mi 2990.8) | off. mi 2999.6 | NM | NM map 7 | A 24-hour Walmart Supercenter, several dollar stores and motels on I-10, thirty miles north of Columbus on NM 11. The full-grocery backstop for the Columbus alternate, and listed in the older TrailQuest address set as a box town. Not on any version of the trail: it is a bus or a hitch from Columbus or Lordsburg, and the accessFrom point here is the NM 9 crossing only because that is where the alternate begins. Accepts resupply boxes. Post office: Deming, NM 88030 (general delivery). 55 mi off trail by hitching. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <type>town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="31.787474" lon="-108.426747">
    <ele>1433.3</ele>
    <name>Official mile 30</name>
    <desc>mi 2999.1 (SOBO mi 2999.1) | off. mi 3007.9 | NM | NM map 5 | CDTC official mile 30, counted northbound from Crazy Cook. Official SOBO mile 3007.9; geometric SOBO mile 2999.1.</desc>
    <type>milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="31.73388" lon="-108.41075">
    <ele>1331.8</ele>
    <name>Highway 81 water cache</name>
    <desc>mi 3003.2 (SOBO mi 3003.2) | off. mi 3012.0 | NM | NM map 4 | CDTC cache box on NM 81 in the Bootheel, the second box north of Crazy Cook. Stocked for shuttle riders and for the paid water service; otherwise self-cache. Coordinates are CDTC&apos;s own. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <link href="https://cdtcoalition.org/explore-the-trail/southern-terminus-shuttle/" />
    <type>water</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="31.668059" lon="-108.364429">
    <ele>1444.1</ele>
    <name>Official mile 20</name>
    <desc>mi 3009.1 (SOBO mi 3009.1) | off. mi 3017.9 | NM | NM map 3 | CDTC official mile 20, counted northbound from Crazy Cook. Official SOBO mile 3017.9; geometric SOBO mile 3009.1.</desc>
    <type>milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="31.640363" lon="-108.33999">
    <ele>1471.9</ele>
    <name>Antelope Wells leaves the CDT</name>
    <desc>mi 3012.0 (SOBO mi 3012.0) | off. mi 3020.8 | NM | NM map 3 | Antelope Wells: 30.2 mi against 11.8 mi on the CDT, +1,929 ft. OSM relation 7937900 &apos;Antelope Wells Route to Mexico&apos; (ref:ley &apos;NM NM 41&apos;, ref &apos;un41&apos;), 45.1 mi. The alternate southern terminus at the Antelope Wells port of entry on NM-81 - the pre-Crazy-Cook finish, still used because it has a road and a border post. Ley&apos;s NM 41a: &apos;The alternates are all old routes that can come in handy if you want to climb Big Hatchet Peak, go to Antelope Wells, or to Hachita.&apos;</desc>
    <type>junction</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="31.6124" lon="-108.31332">
    <ele>1482.5</ele>
    <name>Sheridan Canyon water cache</name>
    <desc>mi 3014.7 (SOBO mi 3014.7) | off. mi 3023.6 | NM | NM map 3 | The first CDTC cache box north of the Crazy Cook southern terminus, and the one that matters most - there is nothing else between it and the border monument. Stocked for shuttle riders and for the paid water service; otherwise self-cache before you start. Coordinates are CDTC&apos;s own. Checked 2026-09.</desc>
    <link href="https://cdtcoalition.org/explore-the-trail/southern-terminus-shuttle/" />
    <type>water</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="31.572119" lon="-108.328885">
    <ele>1602.9</ele>
    <name>Official mile 10</name>
    <desc>mi 3019.0 (SOBO mi 3019.0) | off. mi 3027.9 | NM | NM map 2 | CDTC official mile 10, counted northbound from Crazy Cook. Official SOBO mile 3027.9; geometric SOBO mile 3019.0.</desc>
    <type>milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="31.497064" lon="-108.208509">
    <ele>1309</ele>
    <name>Southern terminus - Crazy Cook</name>
    <desc>mi 3029.0 (SOBO mi 3029.0) | off. mi 3037.9 | New Mexico | NM map 1 | The Crazy Cook monument on the Mexican border in the New Mexico bootheel. Southbound finish; northbound mile 0. No road access without a shuttle.</desc>
    <type>endpoint</type>
  </wpt>
